Ex. No: 5

INSTALLATION OF HIVE ALONG WITH PRACTICE EXAMPLES

Date:

AIM:

To write a program for the installation of Hive along with practice examples.

PROCEDURE:

Step 1: Verifying Java Installation

Java must be installed on your system before installing Hive. Verify Java installation using the following command:

java -version

If Java is not installed, download the JDK and extract it using the following commands:

cd Downloads/
ls
tar zxf jdk-7u71-linux-x64.gz

Move Java to "/usr/local/":

su
mv jdk1.7.0_71 /usr/local/
exit

Set the environment variables in "~/.bashrc":

export JAVA_HOME=/usr/local/jdk1.7.0_71
export PATH=$PATH:$JAVA_HOME/bin
source ~/.bashrc

Verify the installation:

java -version

Step 2: Verifying Hadoop Installation

Verify Hadoop installation using:

hadoop version

If Hadoop is not installed, download and extract Hadoop 2.4.1.

Set the Hadoop environment variables in "~/.bashrc":

export HADOOP_HOME=/usr/local/hadoop
export HADOOP_MAPRED_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export HADOOP_COMMON_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export HADOOP_HDFS_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export YARN_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export PATH=$PATH:$HADOOP_HOME/sbin:$HADOOP_HOME/bin
source ~/.bashrc

Configure the Hadoop files:

- "core-site.xml"
- "hdfs-site.xml"
- "yarn-site.xml"
- "mapred-site.xml"

Format the NameNode:

hdfs namenode -format

Start Hadoop services:

start-dfs.sh
start-yarn.sh

Step 3: Downloading Hive

Download the Hive archive and verify it using:

cd Downloads
ls

Step 4: Installing Hive

Extract the Hive archive:

tar zxvf apache-hive-0.14.0-bin.tar.gz
ls

Move the extracted files to "/usr/local/hive":

su -
mv apache-hive-0.14.0-bin /usr/local/hive
exit

Set the Hive environment variables in "~/.bashrc":

export HIVE_HOME=/usr/local/hive
export PATH=$PATH:$HIVE_HOME/bin
export CLASSPATH=$CLASSPATH:/usr/local/hadoop/lib/*:.
export CLASSPATH=$CLASSPATH:/usr/local/hive/lib/*:.
source ~/.bashrc

Step 5: Configuring Hive

Open the Hive configuration directory:

cd $HIVE_HOME/conf
cp hive-env.sh.template hive-env.sh

Add the following line to "hive-env.sh":

export HADOOP_HOME=/usr/local/hadoop

Step 6: Downloading and Installing Apache Derby

Download and extract Apache Derby:

wget http://archive.apache.org/dist/db/derby/db-derby-10.4.2.0/db-derby-10.4.2.0-bin.tar.gz
tar zxvf db-derby-10.4.2.0-bin.tar.gz

Move Derby to "/usr/local/derby":

su -
mv db-derby-10.4.2.0-bin /usr/local/derby
exit

Set the Derby environment variables:

export DERBY_HOME=/usr/local/derby
export PATH=$PATH:$DERBY_HOME/bin
export CLASSPATH=$CLASSPATH:$DERBY_HOME/lib/derby.jar:$DERBY_HOME/lib/derbytools.jar
source ~/.bashrc

Create a directory to store Metastore data:

mkdir $DERBY_HOME/data

Step 7: Configuring Metastore of Hive

Open the Hive configuration directory:

cd $HIVE_HOME/conf
cp hive-default.xml.template hive-site.xml

Add the following property between the "<configuration>" tags in "hive-site.xml":

<property>
  <name>javax.jdo.option.ConnectionURL</name>
  <value>jdbc:derby://localhost:1527/metastore_db;create=true</value>
  <description>JDBC connect string for a JDBC metastore</description>
</property>

Create a file named "jpox.properties" and configure the required properties.

Step 8: Verifying Hive Installation

Create the required HDFS directories and set permissions:

hadoop fs -mkdir /tmp
hadoop fs -mkdir /user/hive/warehouse
hadoop fs -chmod g+w /tmp
hadoop fs -chmod g+w /user/hive/warehouse

Start Hive:

cd $HIVE_HOME
bin/hive

To display all tables:

SHOW TABLES;

HIVE EXAMPLES

OBJECTIVE:

Use Hive to create, alter, and drop databases, tables, views, functions, and indexes.

PROGRAM:

1. Database Creation

CREATE DATABASE database_name;

2. Drop Database

DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS database_name CASCADE;

3. Creating a Table

CREATE TABLE table_name (
    id INT,
    name STRING
);

4. Loading Data into a Table

LOAD DATA LOCAL INPATH '<path>/u.data'
OVERWRITE INTO TABLE u_data;

5. Alter Table

Rename a table:

ALTER TABLE name RENAME TO new_name;

Add columns:

ALTER TABLE name ADD COLUMNS (age INT);

Change a column:

ALTER TABLE name CHANGE column_name new_name STRING;

6. Creating and Dropping a View

Create a view:

CREATE VIEW view_name AS
SELECT * FROM table_name;

Drop a view:

DROP VIEW view_name;

7. Functions in Hive

String functions:

- "round()"
- "ceil()"
- "substr()"
- "upper()"
- "reg_exp()"

Date and time functions:

- "year()"
- "month()"
- "day()"
- "to_date()"

Aggregate functions:

- "sum()"
- "min()"
- "max()"
- "count()"
- "avg()"

8. Creating an Index

CREATE INDEX index_ip
ON TABLE log_data(ip_address)
AS 'org.apache.hadoop.hive.ql.index.compact.CompactIndexHandler'
WITH DEFERRED REBUILD;

9. Altering and Rebuilding an Index

ALTER INDEX index_ip_address
ON log_data REBUILD;

10. Dropping an Index

DROP INDEX INDEX_NAME ON TABLE_NAME;

RESULT:

Thus, the program for the installation of Hive along with practice examples was written, executed, and verified successfully.
